## 1. Re-test the prior assumption

State the assumed blocker in one sentence, then write the **executable repro**
that proves or refutes it. Most "blockers" are environment artifacts.

```
$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' <endpoint>
200
```

Escalate to a TLS-impersonating client only if the naive client fails:

```
$ python3 -c "from curl_cffi import requests; print(requests.get('<url>', impersonate='chrome').status_code)"
200
```

If neither passes, name the actual blocker (Cloudflare Turnstile, app-only
OTP, paid subscription wall, etc.) and stop here. Document it for the human.

